WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.534
-You had a very stressful year.
-Oh, yeah.

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:02.635
-I know everything is okay now.
-Yeah.

00:00:02.635 --> 00:00:05.138 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But your wife in April
had a brain tumor removed.

00:00:05.138 --> 00:00:06.740 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes. It was...
-And she is recovering okay?

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:10.777 align:start size:94% position:6%
She's great. She's backstage.
She's doing great.

00:00:10.777 --> 00:00:12.112 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So thank you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:12.112 --> 00:00:14.447 size:84% position:42%
-So happy to hear that.
-Yeah, no, it was...

00:00:14.447 --> 00:00:17.550
It was, I mean, you know, I joke
around about it in my act

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:20.320 align:start size:94% position:6%
and everything, but it
was really scary for a while

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:21.287 line:92%
'cause we have five kids.

00:00:21.287 --> 00:00:22.322 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And there were moments when

00:00:22.322 --> 00:00:25.558
I was like, oh, my gosh,
if anything happens to my wife,

00:00:25.558 --> 00:00:28.528
those five kids are gonna be put
up for adoption.

00:00:28.528 --> 00:00:30.497 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:30.497 --> 00:00:31.197 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
You know?

00:00:31.197 --> 00:00:34.100 align:start size:94% position:6%
Some of these jokes are just
for the fathers.

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:36.569 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
But no, she's doing great,

00:00:36.569 --> 00:00:39.539 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, you know, we are,
you know, really grateful.

00:00:39.539 --> 00:00:41.074 align:start size:94% position:6%
She had an amazing team
of doctors.

00:00:41.074 --> 00:00:44.377 align:start size:94% position:6%
She had a brain surgeon
we found later -- later on.

00:00:44.377 --> 00:00:46.246 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was -- he was the best.
-Uh-huh.

00:00:46.246 --> 00:00:51.418
-I don't know how they determine
who the best brain surgeon is.

00:00:51.418 --> 00:00:53.787 align:start size:94% position:6%
Maybe there's a competition,
you know?

00:00:53.787 --> 00:00:54.687 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.687 --> 00:00:56.790 align:start size:94% position:6%
"America's Got Tumors"
or something.

00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:57.557 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:57.557 --> 00:01:00.860
And Heidi Klum thought,
you know, why does someone have

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:02.896 align:start size:94% position:6%
to be the best brain surgeon?
-Yeah.

00:01:02.896 --> 00:01:06.433 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Isn't it enough that
they're a brain surgeon?

00:01:06.433 --> 00:01:06.966 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:06.966 --> 00:01:10.403 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, none of us could even
get in med school.

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:14.207 align:start size:94% position:6%
This guy went to med school,
graduated,

00:01:14.207 --> 00:01:16.076 size:88% position:44% line:92%
specialized in the brain

00:01:16.076 --> 00:01:19.245 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then specialized
in brain surgery,

00:01:19.245 --> 00:01:22.148 align:start size:94% position:6%
and people are, like, yeah,
but is he any good?

00:01:22.148 --> 00:01:25.552 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
Yeah! He -- he's good!

00:01:25.552 --> 00:01:27.821 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know what they do
with the bad brain surgeons?

00:01:27.821 --> 00:01:30.623 align:start size:94% position:6%
They don't let them
be brain surgeons.

00:01:30.623 --> 00:01:32.592 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:32.592 --> 00:01:33.460 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
But, uh...

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:35.728 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cheers and applause ]
Thank you.

00:01:35.728 --> 00:01:39.165 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's -- it's really impressive
when you think about it.

00:01:39.165 --> 00:01:42.001 size:81% position:41%
Like, a brain surgeon,
they can never relax.

00:01:42.001 --> 00:01:44.704 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, at no point
when they're at work,

00:01:44.704 --> 00:01:46.673 align:start size:94% position:6%
can they say,
"hey, it ain't brain surgery."

00:01:46.673 --> 00:01:49.576 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
Because it's brain surgery.

00:01:49.576 --> 00:01:51.678 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah. [ Laughs ]

00:01:51.678 --> 00:01:52.846 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you think, look,
if you were a doctor,

00:01:52.846 --> 00:01:54.747
what kind of doctor do you think
you would be?

00:01:54.747 --> 00:01:56.749 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, I had some time to think
about this.

00:01:56.749 --> 00:01:59.152 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think I would want to be
an anesthesiologist...

00:01:59.152 --> 00:02:00.720 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh-huh.
-...because I just would like

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:04.023 align:start size:94% position:6%
to walk into a room and say,
Hi. I'm Dr. Gaffigan.

00:02:04.023 --> 00:02:07.594
I'm going to give you some drugs
so you can't talk or move.

00:02:07.594 --> 00:02:09.996
[ Laughter ]
And then one of these strangers

00:02:09.996 --> 00:02:11.664 line:92%
is going to cut you open.

00:02:11.664 --> 00:02:13.333 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
Good luck with that.

00:02:13.333 --> 00:02:17.203
I mean, what would draw someone
to anesthesiology?

00:02:17.203 --> 00:02:19.539 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's like, I like medicine,
but I really enjoy

00:02:19.539 --> 00:02:22.075 align:start size:94% position:6%
getting people high.
-[ Laughs ] Yeah.

00:02:22.075 --> 00:02:24.577 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So if I could combine
those two.

00:02:24.577 --> 00:02:26.980 align:start size:94% position:6%
I also prefer to sit
during surgery.

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:28.414 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. [ Laughs ]
-I love how

00:02:28.414 --> 00:02:29.482 align:start size:94% position:6%
the anesthesiologists
during surgery --

00:02:29.482 --> 00:02:30.550 align:start size:94% position:6%
they're always sitting there,
like,

00:02:30.550 --> 00:02:32.552 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I don't even know why I have
to be here."

00:02:32.552 --> 00:02:34.320 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:36.422 line:92%
"Yeah, they're still alive."

00:02:36.422 --> 00:02:38.158 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
"I wish I had my phone."

00:02:38.158 --> 00:02:41.761 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And is this something that
while you're going through it,

00:02:41.761 --> 00:02:43.997
how quickly did you start
making jokes about it?

00:02:43.997 --> 00:02:46.065 align:start size:94% position:6%
Obviously, your wife knows who
she's married to...

00:02:46.065 --> 00:02:47.967 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-But was this a case where

00:02:47.967 --> 00:02:49.736 line:92%
as soon as the tumor came up,

00:02:49.736 --> 00:02:51.905 align:start size:94% position:6%
you were coming up
with tumor comedy?

00:02:51.905 --> 00:02:55.441
Well, there is something.
I should preface this by saying

00:02:55.441 --> 00:02:57.343 align:start size:94% position:6%
my wife is my writing partner,
so...

00:02:57.343 --> 00:02:59.412 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
-You know, she got out

00:02:59.412 --> 00:03:02.248 align:start size:94% position:6%
of a 2-hour MRI,
and, like, the first thing

00:03:02.248 --> 00:03:05.018
she said to me is like,
"Write down these jokes."

00:03:05.018 --> 00:03:05.552 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:05.552 --> 00:03:09.255 size:84% position:42%
So these are, you know,
this is, I mean, she,

00:03:09.255 --> 00:03:11.624
you know, you have to have
a sense of humor about this.

00:03:11.624 --> 00:03:14.928 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, it's just, you know,
it's something, you know,

00:03:14.928 --> 00:03:16.729 align:start size:94% position:6%
but you have to be delicate
about it,

00:03:16.729 --> 00:03:19.799
like, you can't really complain
around someone

00:03:19.799 --> 00:03:20.567 line:92%
who has had a brain tumor.

00:03:20.567 --> 00:03:23.036
You can't -- you know, my wife's
not the type to bring it up.

00:03:23.036 --> 00:03:24.637 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, once, she did.
She was like, "You know,

00:03:24.637 --> 00:03:26.472 align:start size:94% position:6%
I had a brain tumor,"
but I couldn't say anything.

00:03:26.472 --> 00:03:29.075
I couldn't be like, "yeah,
that was, like, a month ago."

00:03:29.075 --> 00:03:30.944 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ] Right.
-You know?

00:03:30.944 --> 00:03:32.011 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:32.011 --> 00:03:35.615 size:81% position:41%
What about my seasonal
allergies? You know?

00:03:35.615 --> 00:03:37.450 align:start size:94% position:6%
They were pretty tough
this year.

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:40.954 align:start size:94% position:6%
But she's got an amazing sense
of humor, so...

